            "G": "Use the 0.0270 s C candidate as the current measured incumbent; the baseline is 0.0690 s. Compare complete candidate programs under the same correctness and timing procedure, retaining the fastest valid result. Do not assume individually successful changes combine additively: test any integration directly. Preserve input handling, generated values, signed ordering, sortedness validation, and the exact MD5 output; do not alter the harness or build constraints.",
            "analysis": "The baseline is valid at 0.0690 s. The best observed candidate is C at 0.0270 s (~2.55× faster); A's best is 0.0355 s and another C candidate is 0.0474 s. The measured is_sorted SIMD changes are effectively neutral or slower (0.0688–0.0701 s), so further effort should target sorting rather than repeat those changes. The ARM64 target has four cores. All candidates must still sort the actual generated data correctly and produce the same checksum; the supplied example or any particular test values are not optimization assumptions."
