          "plan": {
            "A": "Research hot-loop optimizations while retaining the existing exact step-by-step BFS: precompute per-cell movement neighbors, reduce box-occupancy checks, and replace bubble sorting of box positions with a cheaper canonicalization method. Preserve state identity and shortest-path behavior. Benchmark each change independently against the baseline and retain it only if it improves measured time without correctness regressions.",
            "B": "Research visited-state and memory-layout optimizations: avoid unnecessary full-coordinate comparisons by checking stored hashes first, assess hash quality and table growth, and compare state/frontier storage approaches. Keep collision handling exact and ensure canonical box ordering remains consistent. Measure changes independently; do not assume combining individually promising changes will help.",
            "C": "Investigate search-order correctness and sound search-space reduction. The specification requires the shortest solution with up, down, left, right tie order, while the current move generator uses a different order and prepends states to each frontier; evaluate an order-preserving FIFO BFS and verify its output. Separately assess only sound, general deadlock pruning or an exact weighted push-level search; preserve minimum player moves and tie order, and do not adopt an abstraction that loses required path information. Check board-boundary handling as part of correctness.",
            "G": "Integrate the strongest independently measured A/B/C candidates, resolving overlap without reverting others' work. Validate the integrated program against the supplied correctness oracle and exact shortest/tie-order requirements on all available cases, then measure the combined integration against the baseline on the ARM64 4-core target. Combination performance may be worse than individual candidates; keep only changes supported by integrated measurements and preserve correctness for general valid inputs.",
            "analysis": "Evidence is limited to one valid baseline: 4/4 cases correct, mean runtime 0.004945 seconds, score 0.5, on ARM64 with 4 CPU cores and no GPU. No candidate measurements are available, so these are research directions rather than predicted gains. The source uses per-step BFS with sorted box positions, a custom chained hash table, and static reverse-push dead-square marking; its move order/frontier insertion do not visibly implement the statement's specified tie order. Prioritize exact correctness and independent measurements; do not specialize to test cases or replace the computation."
