            "analysis": "This is Problem D: the source stores fixed-capacity string records, groups by first character, sorts each group with strcmp, then prints the strings. The baseline is correct on its reported cases and averages 0.42005 s; admissible variants measure 0.01303–0.01444 s, roughly 29–32× faster by those means. The fastest is the sharded C candidate, but its shown parallel loops share `i`, so its timing is not sufficient evidence of a safe implementation. The next-fastest C candidate uses serial counting/scattering and parallel qsort. Candidate correctness details are not included in the measurements, so verify correctness rather than infer it from speed."
