            "analysis": "The official task counts submatrices summing to k, with dimensions below 1000 and potentially negative entries. The baseline is correct at 0.2500 s. The strongest measured candidate is 9661742815304083 at 0.0715 s (about 3.5× the baseline speedup), using shorter-dimension pairing, contiguous scans, and a generation-stamped hash table. The measured OpenMP version is 0.0962 s; other listed variants are about 0.2296–0.2482 s. Thus research should start from the serial winner, test alternatives empirically, and make no assumption that optimizations compose."
